{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155263-homebrew-magic-system-for-sleepwalkers","id":1155263,"title":"Homebrew Magic System for Sleepwalkers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-02T19:55:45-07:00","id":1155263,"title":"Homebrew Magic System for Sleepwalkers","content":"So while my Discord was still fresh, and one of my first members to join - 'Azrabael' was apparently having some issues getting in, said something like the app was cloning him, I asked &quot;What kind of arcana do you need for that?&quot; And being silly, I put<br /> <br /> Phone \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> And something occurred to me.<br /> <br /> What if there can be something like a 'fallen' arcanum? It could literally be anything. Like Car \u2022\u2022 or Snake \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> Something like this could be a way for people who 'get it' could get some meager shadow of the magic that the awakened wield. I was reminded of the Gutter Magic system that was presented in Hunter the Vigil (the sourcebook about Witches)<br /> <br /> Suppose that with proper tutoring, a Sleepwalker can get access to magic in a limited way, using these fallen arcana? Their central power attribute would be something like their ability to even form an imago. While the imago is basically a mage's default and natural bread and butter, it can be the one thing that a sleepwalker struggles to become proficient in. With practice, she can do it, and it solely makes her able to just do a magical casting. But only with the most surface symbols. While an Awakened who touched the Supernal gets the Supernal Arcana, the ten umbrella concepts that arc over the entire tellurian, the sleepwalker must be limited to only the fallen aspects that she can understand. Essentially, take any Platonian symbol and make that an 'arcanum' that she can become proficient in, only affecting things in those purviews.<br /> <br /> So in sum: A sleepwalker - with training under the wing of an Awakened mentor, can be taught how to strive to make a crude imago, to cast a spell under the purview of a shallow symbol, like Computer, Door, or Jewelry.<br /> <br /> Such magic is probably highly situational, but it's a start.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>..............","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21103-mindflower","name":"Mindflower","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T20:08:38-07:00","id":1155266,"title":"","content":"So, basically a mortal with Influences?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T10:27:42-07:00","id":1155440,"title":"","content":"While nothing stops you from houseruling this into your game... that is really not how sleepwalkers or magic works in awakening. If you want to give sleepwalkers supernatural powers I personally recommend giving them any of the established supernatural merits (second sight from 1e also has a lot in that regard) or using proximi, which are actually touched by the supernal.<br /> <br /> If you want to give mortals influences you can do that via spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T11:44:32-07:00","id":1155804,"title":"","content":"Why would you not just use Gutter Magic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T13:46:41-07:00","id":1155841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1155263-homebrew-magic-system-for-sleepwalkers?p=1155804#post1155804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would 